1
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:58,500
Cultures collide. Hope survives.

2
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:51,000
American Factory is a documentary film directed by Steven Bognar.

3
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:43,500
In post-industrial Ohio, a Chinese billionaire opens a new factory in the husk of an
abandoned General Motors plant, hiring two thousand blue-collar Americans.

4
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Early days of hope and optimism give way to setbacks as
high-tech China clashes with working-class America.

5
00:34:22,500 --> 00:34:28,500
Self - Vice President, Fuyao, played by Junming 'Jimmy' Wang.

6
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Self - U.S. Senator, Ohio, played by Sherrod Brown.

7
00:48:07,500 --> 00:48:13,500
Self - Vice President, Fuyao Glass America, played by Dave Burrows.

8
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Self - President, Fuyao Glass America, played by John Gauthier.

9
01:01:52,500 --> 01:01:58,500
Self - Furnace Supervisor, played by Rob Haerr.

10
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
Self - Lamination Specialist, played by Cynthia Harper.

11
01:15:37,500 --> 01:15:43,500
American Factory (Chinese: 美国工厂) is a 2019 American documentary film directed by Steven Bognar and Julia Reichert, about Chinese company
Fuyao's factory in Moraine, a city near Dayton, Ohio, that occupies Moraine Assembly, a shuttered General Motors plant.

12
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The film had its festival premiere at the 2019 Sundance Film Festival.

13
01:29:22,500 --> 01:29:28,500
It is distributed by Netflix, and is the first film acquired by Barack and
Michelle Obama's production company, Higher Ground Productions.

14
01:36:15,000 --> 01:36:21,000
At the 92nd Academy Awards, American Factory won the
award for Best Documentary Feature.

15
01:43:07,500 --> 01:43:13,500
The film explores themes of factory worker,
culture clash, ohio, chinese, american.
